    "text": "The selected hotspot workgroup has 16\u00d78 invocations and computes a 64-output-channel by 64-output-position tile. Each invocation retains eight vec4 accumulators (32 FP32 results). The target has K=128\u00d711=1408, split into 44 K32 tiles.\n\nEach K tile cooperatively loads 512 A vec4 values and 512 B vec4 values: 8KiB each, 16KiB logical global-load payload per workgroup, before cache reuse. Shared storage is sa[32][64] float plus sb[32][16] vec4, also exactly16KiB. Each invocation owns four preload iterations of each array. Packed A arrives as channel-vector vec4 and is scattered to four scalar shared locations; B keeps its vector layout. This is logical issued payload, not measured physical DRAM traffic.\n\nFor every k, a thread loads eight A scalars and four B scalars (native two A vec4 LDS plus one B vec4 LDS), and performs32 scalar MADs. A K32 tile therefore issues1024 MADs and96 vec4 shared loads per invocation, or131072 MADs/262144 FLOPs per workgroup. Reuse across the64\u00d764 tile is the reason the16KiB preload serves far more shared-read/arithmetic work. Two barriers bracket each tile. Output is written once after all44 tiles; bias/activation follow the dot accumulation.\n\nThe actual selected and unroll4 targets both allocate16 full vector registers, no half registers and no private storage. Their128-thread combined footprint is4096, exactly the retained admission bound; the32 scalar accumulators occupy eight full vec4 registers of that footprint. Unroll4 retains residency and arithmetic/shared-load counts but expands the native body and adds nine hot-loop MOVs per four k steps. It reduced four-step expanded issue count220\u2192172, yet the twelve actual command walls increased.\n\nMatched fcd rd_queue.c:233 and pinned Gallium a5xx/fd5_compute.c:28 explicitly set hardware INSTRLEN=0 for v->instrlen>32. This clears SP_CS_CTRL_REG0.BUFFER and omits CP_LOAD_STATE4 shader preload. Selected native27/28 remains in that preload path; unroll4 native35 (4480-byte rounded instruction footprint) switches out. This is direct source evidence of a changed fetch mode at32\u00d7128=4096 bytes, not a proof of physical instruction-cache capacity, miss counts or causal attribution of the measured slowdown. Other code/loop and resource effects coexist; swap also differed0\u219223.9MiB.\n\nThe separate unroll2 source preserves all data movement, output layouts, original B division and exact arithmetic order. Its prospective native gate requires <=32units so it can test reduced loop overhead while retaining the original preload path. No driver threshold, batching, register or safety limit is changed.\n",
    "limitation": "Driver emission mode change is proven; physical cache capacity, misses, and timing causality are not."
